Package: dicomr
Type: Package
Title: Read, Write and Decode DICOM Medical Image Files
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Matt", "Segar", email = "cscswimmer227@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph")),
    person("Darcy", "Mason", role = c("ctb", "cph"),
           comment = "author of 'pydicom', from which the DICOM data dictionary is derived"),
    person("pydicom contributors", role = c("ctb", "cph"),
           comment = "DICOM data dictionary derived from 'pydicom'")
  )
Description: A native reader and writer for DICOM (Digital Imaging and
    Communications in Medicine) files, the standard format for medical
    images, published by the National Electrical Manufacturers Association
    <https://www.dicomstandard.org/current>. Modeled on the 'Python'
    package 'pydicom' and checked against it. Parses the file format in
    C++ (implicit and explicit value representations, both byte
    orders, deflated data sets, nested sequences and encapsulated pixel
    data), gives keyword and tag based access to data elements, writes
    data sets back to disk, and decodes pixel data into R arrays:
    uncompressed, RLE Lossless and JPEG Baseline (through 'libjpeg'), with
    YBR to RGB color conversion. Includes helpers for cardiac and other
    ultrasound, such as calibration from the Sequence of Ultrasound
    Regions and frame timing for cine loops.
